  "summary": "Reconciled all 5 St. Brigid discharges under RBC-TOC-02. Each patient has a progress note, with a correction note where new information arrived while I worked.\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005): Furosemide increased to 40 mg twice daily, as the signed addendum (doc-00009) says (mr-00075 → mr-t0001). Potassium chloride stopped (mr-00076). Omeprazole kept; the hospital's pantoprazole swap was not ordered. Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin unchanged. Lisinopril (mr-00072): I first kept it on hold because potassium was 5.4 on 10/21 and made task-t0003 for you. A repeat BMP from 10/23 (doc-00901: K 4.7, SCr 1.21) then arrived, so I resumed lisinopril per the discharge condition. I couldn't close task-t0003 with my tools; please disregard it (I messaged you, comm-t0019). An unsigned draft addendum proposing furosemide 60 mg twice daily (doc-00902) was not acted on.\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004): Carvedilol is unchanged at 6.25 mg twice daily. I first raised it to 12.5 mg per the summary, but a signed addendum (doc-00904) reversed that for heart rate 48–52 and lightheadedness on standing, so it is back at 6.25 mg (mr-t0016). Insulin 70/30 and aspirin unchanged. FLAGGED TO YOU:\n(1) Atorvastatin 80 mg: fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission, with none since 03/04 (comm-t0006). No change made.\n(2) Glipizide 5 mg from Dr. Desai at Valley Endocrinology: filled at an outside pharmacy, not in our orders and not mentioned at discharge. No order placed. Please clarify, since he's also on insulin (comm-t0007).\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044): Insulin glargine, insulin lispro and rosuvastatin unchanged. Lisinopril (mr-00373) is ON HOLD. I first resumed it on the 10/22 BMP (SCr 1.08, K 4.6). Then a potassium of 5.5 from 10/23 (obs-09002) arrived, so I put it back on hold. FLAGGED: task-t0018 for you, due 10/26, for a repeat potassium and the decision on lisinopril.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069): Lisinopril 20 mg resumed (mr-69003), since post-discharge SCr was 1.12 (needed under 1.5) and K 4.4. Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged. The discharge plan called for a potassium 3 days after discharge, but I found none in the chart.\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067): Metformin ER stays ON HOLD. The only creatinine on file (1.21) is from the hospital stay, and the condition requires a post-discharge result. FLAGGED: task-t0013 for you, due 10/24, when the post-discharge BMP is expected. Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nI closed the four inbox items for results and documents that arrived during the work, each linked to the action taken.",
